      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n-----\n\n\nIn `bootrom.cc`, functions like `GetBootromInfo`, `GetFlashInfo`, and `ReadReg` repeatedly do this dance:\n\n1. Initialize a `req` struct.  \n2. `SendStruct(req)`.  \n3. Check for error.  \n4. `ReadStruct\u003cResponse\u003e`.  \n5. Check for error.  \n6. Return data.\n\nYou already implemented `SendCommandTyped\u003cT\u003e` in `EcComm` to solve exactly this problem\\! You can do the exact same thing in `BootromComm`:\n\n```c\n// Add to BootromComm\ntemplate \u003cTriviallyCopyable Resp, TriviallyCopyable Req\u003e\nstd::expected\u003cResp, BootromError\u003e SendAndReadStruct(const Req\u0026 req) {\n  auto resp \u003d SendStruct(req);\n  if (!resp) return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n  \n  auto parsed \u003d ReadStruct\u003cResp\u003e(*resp);\n  if (!parsed) return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n  return parsed.value();\n}\n\n```\n\nNow `GetBootromInfo` becomes incredibly concise:\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cEgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::GetBootromInfo() {\n  auto info_res \u003d SendAndReadStruct\u003cEgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse\u003e(\n      EgisBootrom::GetBootromInfoCommand{});\n      \n  if (info_res) {\n    info_res-\u003eversion \u003d FromLittleEndian(info_res-\u003eversion);\n    info_res-\u003emax_cmd_size \u003d FromLittleEndian(info_res-\u003emax_cmd_size);\n    info_res-\u003emax_fw_upgrade_size \u003d FromLittleEndian(info_res-\u003emax_fw_upgrade_size);\n  }\n  return info_res;\n}\n\n```",
