      "message": "The style guide generally forbids assignments inside `if`, `while`, or `switch` conditions because they are visually confusing and error-prone, unless the variable is being newly declared in that exact scope (e.g., `while (int x \u003d ...)`).\n\nIn **`cli_options.cc`**, the CLI parsing loop relies on a traditional C-style `getopt` idiom:\n\n```c\nint opt;\nwhile ((opt \u003d getopt_long_only(argc, argv, \"f:c:a:k:o:s:d:p:h\", long_options,\n                               nullptr)) !\u003d -1) {\n\n```\n\n**Fix:** Extract the assignment to prioritize readability and strict compliance:\n\n```c\nwhile (true) {\n  int opt \u003d getopt_long_only(argc, argv, \"f:c:a:k:o:s:d:p:h\", long_options, nullptr);\n  if (opt \u003d\u003d -1) {\n    break;\n  }\n  switch (opt) {\n    // ...\n\n```",
