      "writtenOn": "2026-06-15T21:46:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `egis_util.h`, `ReadLittleEndian` is an exact duplicate of `ReadStruct`, with the only difference being the call to `FromLittleEndian`.\n\nBecause you are using C++23, `std::expected` has a `.transform()` monadic operation. You can completely eliminate the duplicated `memcpy` and bounds-checking logic by routing `ReadLittleEndian` through `ReadStruct`.\n\n**In `egis_util.h`:**\n\n```c\n// Replace the current ReadLittleEndian with this 1-liner:\ntemplate \u003cstd::integral T\u003e\nstd::expected\u003cT, std::errc\u003e ReadLittleEndian(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e buffer, \n                                             size_t offset \u003d 0) {\n  return ReadStruct\u003cT\u003e(buffer, offset).transform(FromLittleEndian\u003cT\u003e);\n}\n\n```",
