      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn `egis_util.h`, `PackMessage` uses the pre-C++23 idiom of calling `.insert()` with `begin()` and `end()` iterators to concatenate data.\n\nC++23 introduced `.append_range()`, which accepts `std::span` (or any range) directly. This removes the iterator boilerplate and clearly expresses your intent:\n\n**Before:**\n\n```c\ntemplate \u003cTriviallyCopyable T\u003e\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e PackMessage(const T \u0026header, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e payload \u003d {}) {\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e buffer;\n  buffer.reserve(sizeof(T) + payload.size());\n  \n  auto header_bytes \u003d AsBytes(header);\n  buffer.insert(buffer.end(), header_bytes.begin(), header_bytes.end());\n  buffer.insert(buffer.end(), payload.begin(), payload.end());\n  \n  return buffer;\n}\n\n```\n\n**After:**\n\n```c\ntemplate \u003cTriviallyCopyable T\u003e\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e PackMessage(const T \u0026header, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e payload \u003d {}) {\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e buffer;\n  buffer.reserve(sizeof(T) + payload.size());\n  \n  buffer.append_range(AsBytes(header));\n  buffer.append_range(payload);\n  \n  return buffer;\n}\n\n```",
